    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on high-upside speed threats and top-of-the-order hitters. **Trea Turner** (81.27) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) headline our lineup as the premier plays; **Trea Turner** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Abbott\u2019s 5.07 xERA and a premier leadoff spot, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** finds himself in an ideal confluence of variables, boasting a +16% park factor and a +4% boost due to a slow delivery pitcher, making him a major candidate for a multi-steal game. **Kyle Schwarber** (79.42) rounds out this elite tier, leveraging a strong platoon edge against a lefty and a favorable batting order to project as a must-start staple.\n\nEfficiency dictates our focus on platoon advantages and situational speed. **Colt Keith** (68.36) remains a high-value play thanks to a +7% platoon boost, while **Christian Yelich** (60.12) is effectively utilized in the UTIL slot, as his +13% dynamic platoon edge against Dobbins mitigates any concerns regarding park factors. The most difficult personnel decision today involved **Nelson Velazquez** (54.12); despite an elite 0.418 xwOBA, his limited room for efficiency compared to the 60+ rated players kept him on the bench. We are wary of the matchup for **Yordan Alvarez** (49.70), whose raw talent is currently stifled by a difficult 3.11 xERA pitcher and a suboptimal L/L platoon, though his elite 0.479 xwOBA ensures he remains a threat to overperform his modest score. Managers should note that while **Dillon Dingler** and **Gary Sanchez** occupy our catcher slots, their lower scores highlight the inherent volatility of the position; we are prioritizing the rest of the lineup to carry our Roto categories today.",
